  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "The current best (config_003, acc=0.639) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder with resnet50, avgpool, and weighted fusion. We have strong evidence that pca_n2000 beats scgpt (0.639 vs 0.525), avgpool beats transformer (0.639 vs 0.573), and weighted beats concat (0.639 vs 0.619), but scvi_n200 has never been tested in this optimal multimodal/multiprofile setup. Config_022 changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 while keeping all other settings at their best-known values, making it a clean single-variable test. This is the most important remaining uncertainty: whether a learned generative RNA representation can match or exceed the simple PCA baseline. With 4 experiments left after this one, confirming or ruling out scvi_n200 is critical—if it performs competitively, it opens a new promising axis; if not, it consolidates our confidence in pca_n200 and lets us focus remaining budget on marginal gains (e.g., vit_l + weighted fusion at 0.635). This is the highest-information, lowest-risk next step."
}

